# Files the template-sync workflow must never overwrite in derived repos.
# Everything NOT listed here is treated as template-owned and kept in sync;
# conflicts with local edits surface in the sync PR for review. Files that
# exist only downstream (e.g. your src/ tree) are never touched by sync.
#
# Note: per actions-template-sync, this file itself is not synced — each
# derived repo owns its copy and may extend it with project-divergent paths.

# Replaced per project (seed lives in docs/README.template.md)
README.md

# Customized on day 0 with real owners
.github/CODEOWNERS

# Gains project-specific variables downstream
.env.example

# May be relicensed per project
LICENSE

# Project web app (Upskill example-page redesign) — owned downstream, never sync
site/
netlify.toml
docs/upskill/

# Workflow files: the actions-template-sync GitHub App token has no `workflows`
# permission, so GitHub rejects any push that creates/updates .github/workflows/*
# — which fails the ENTIRE sync push (see the template-sync run history). The
# project intentionally stores no PAT secret, so own workflows downstream and
# exclude the whole directory; the rest of the sync (docs, scripts) then succeeds.
# Pull template workflow changes in manually when needed. Covers web-ci.yml and
# the downstream-only pages.yml.
.github/workflows/
